<title>USA: Calif. Assembly votes to block new overtime rule.</title>
<headline>Calif. Assembly votes to block new overtime rule.</headline>
<dateline>SACRAMENTO, Calif. 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>California's Assembly voted Tuesday to reverse controversial employee overtime rules opposed by unions and other labor groups.</p>
<p>The Democrat-controled state Assembly voted 42-to-32 along party lines in favor of Assembly Bill 15, which would overturn the new state rules.</p>
<p>The measure now advances to the Senate for review.</p>
<p>In April, the state Industrial Welfare Commission voted 3-to-2 to change the state's employee overtime policy from an eight-hour work-day standard to a 40-hour work-week standard. The commission said the new rules would take effect January 1.</p>
</text>
